---
description: Never swallow exceptions; at least record them
alwaysApply: true
---

# Never Swallow Exceptions

Do not catch an exception and discard it. Empty `catch` blocks and `catch (… ignored)` with no record of the failure hide bugs.

If the code cannot recover or rethrow, at least write the exception somewhere durable: a log file, `System.err`, or `printStackTrace()`. Prefer a log file under the app's data directory when one exists.

```java
// BAD — silent
} catch (IOException ignored) {
}

// GOOD — recorded
} catch (IOException ex) {
    ex.printStackTrace();
}
```

Catching in tests to assert that a specific exception is thrown is allowed. InterruptedException must still restore the interrupt flag.
